in{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4},\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186387799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387797 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7f87249-b6b1-5efb-aa0a-6f8127d0855d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387798 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨2,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}